From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR=1: a new depth target that the clear binding it covers is not uploaded from guest memory first when the colour targets are smaller (Fritchii EXP56); off by default

Credits. Port of Frizti/Fritchii f93124a6b8 ("texture_cache: EXP56 skips a cleared depth
target's upload; EXP57 caps collector GPU waits", 2026-11-09, EXP56 half only) and 6129793a6b
(EXP56 on by default upstream), by Frizti. Hand port: the upstream diff does not apply here
(Nx2Debug::Experiment, EXP7 log strings). Upstream measured Castle Town 41.3 -> 43.8 fps and its
clear zone 54.7 -> 36.3 ms/s with a live toggle, screenshots off/on identical. Not compiled or
run here.

Why. JoinImages' overwritten_by_clear lets a new render target skip its upload when the clear
that binds it overwrites it whole, but it refuses whenever any bound colour target is smaller
than the new image (the clear only covers the framebuffer's render area). Ocarina of Time binds
a 1920x1024 depth buffer under 1280x720 colour, so its 7.5 MiB depth target is uploaded from guest
memory each time it is made. The PS5 shows it in every Link's-house window: "largest 7 MiB"
uploads, 1,228-1,412 uploads and 323-577 MiB per 600 frames (t98-b run797); village walk 5,351
uploads, 6,151 MiB per 600 frames (t85-f run702). The upload is GPU back-thread work, and the back
thread is the fly-over limit.

EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR=1 (Common::PeSwitch, exact 1; unset or anything else: the old code
path, unchanged).
- overwritten_by_clear skips the smaller-colour-target refusal for the clear's own depth target
  (zeta enabled, zeta address == the new image's address), as upstream. Every other test stays:
  no joins, plain single-level 2D, clear layer 0, the scissor and window-origin tests, the depth
  size test, and the Z / full stencil mask tests by format type.
- The image then stays CpuModified, and UpdateRenderTargets' PrepareImage drops the upload only
  when IsFullClear agrees, as it already does for an existing depth target (IsFullClear ignores
  the colour sizes, same code as upstream). If IsFullClear refuses, PrepareImage uploads after all.
- Relocation (EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_RELOCATE) is unchanged: RelocationCandidate refuses a target larger
  than a bound colour target by its own test. (Upstream's has no such test, so upstream also
  relocates the drifted depth target; here a new image is still made, only its upload goes.)
- With EDEN_UP_SKIP_STALE_UPLOADS=1 such a target takes GuestBytes, as the skipped upload would
  have set it: outside the render area guest memory holds its bytes, so it is never marked stale.
- 600-frame line (with the switch on): "N cleared depth targets over smaller colour targets
  skipped the join upload (M MiB ...)". The first 8 cleared depth targets of 1 MiB or more that
  still took the upload are logged as "Depth clear: ... uploaded: ..." with the clear state
  (EXP7's refusal reasons, as a state dump).

Risk. Texels of the depth target outside the clear's render area hold undefined data instead of
guest bytes, as an existing depth target's already do after a full clear. Only a later use at a
larger render area without a clear could read them.

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index cd2d143..42664fa 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -278,6 +278,21 @@ constexpr u64 KeepRemadeWindow = 600;
     return enabled;
 }
 
+/// EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR=1 (off unless set; Fritchii f93124a6b8 EXP56, on by default
+/// upstream since 6129793a6b): JoinImages' overwritten_by_clear no longer refuses the clear's own
+/// depth target because a bound colour target is smaller. Ocarina of Time binds a 1920x1024 depth
+/// buffer under 1280x720 colour, and that rule uploaded its 7.5 MiB from guest memory each time
+/// the target was made ("largest 7 MiB" in the 600-frame upload line). The image stays
+/// CpuModified, and UpdateRenderTargets' PrepareImage drops the upload when IsFullClear agrees, as
+/// for an existing depth target: texels outside the clear's render area then hold undefined data
+/// instead of guest bytes. With the switch on, the 600-frame lines count the skips, and the first
+/// 8 cleared depth targets of 1 MiB or more that still took the upload are logged with the state
+/// that refused them (EXP7's purpose).
+[[nodiscard]] inline bool FritchiiDepthClear() {
+    static const bool enabled = Common::PeSwitch("EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR");
+    return enabled;
+}
+
 using Tegra::Texture::TICEntry;
 using Tegra::Texture::TSCEntry;
 using VideoCore::Surface::GetFormatType;
@@ -1470,6 +1485,14 @@ void TextureCache<P>::TickFrame() {
                  async_decodes_queued, astc_opaque_images, astc_alpha_images);
         LOG_INFO(HW_GPU, "Texture cache last 600 frames: {} uploads from guest memory, {} MiB (largest {} MiB, {} by layer)",
                  images_uploaded, uploaded_bytes >> 20, largest_upload >> 20, layer_uploads);
+        if (FritchiiDepthClear()) {
+            LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                     "Texture cache last 600 frames: {} cleared depth targets over smaller colour "
+                     "targets skipped the join upload ({} MiB; PrepareImage uploads any that "
+                     "IsFullClear refuses)",
+                     tc_depth_clear_skips, tc_depth_clear_skip_bytes >> 20);
+            tc_depth_clear_skips = tc_depth_clear_skip_bytes = 0;
+        }
         if (NoStaleUpload()) {
             LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
                      "Texture cache last 600 frames: stale uploads skipped {} ({} MiB), {} uploaded "
@@ -5192,7 +5215,10 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
     // A new render target that the clear binding it overwrites whole (every channel, the whole
     // image) needs no upload from guest memory first: Ocarina of Time creates ~4 such targets a
     // frame outdoors, and uploading them was ~15% of the GPU back thread.
+    // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR: set when the depth exemption below decided the result.
+    bool depth_clear_relaxed = false;
     const auto overwritten_by_clear = [&] {
+        depth_clear_relaxed = false;
         if (!clearing_render_targets || !join_copies_to_do.empty() ||
             new_info.type != ImageType::e2D || new_info.resources.levels != 1 ||
             new_info.resources.layers != 1 || new_info.num_samples != 1) {
@@ -5222,10 +5248,19 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
             }
         }
         // The clear covers the framebuffer's render area, the smallest bound target.
+        // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR=1 (Fritchii f93124a6b8, EXP56): not for the clear's own
+        // depth target, which follows IsFullClear as an existing one does (its contents are
+        // dropped, the colour targets' sizes aside).
+        const bool depth_follows_full_clear =
+            FritchiiDepthClear() && regs.zeta_enable && regs.zeta.Address() == gpu_addr;
         for (u32 index = 0; index < regs.rt_control.count && index < NUM_RT; ++index) {
             const auto& rt = regs.rt[index];
             if (rt.Address() != 0 && rt.format != Tegra::RenderTargetFormat::NONE &&
                 (rt.width < width || rt.height < height)) {
+                if (depth_follows_full_clear) {
+                    depth_clear_relaxed = true;
+                    continue;
+                }
                 return false;
             }
         }
@@ -5645,6 +5680,15 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
     if (overwritten_by_clear() && !clear_guard_keeps_upload()) {
         // Stays CpuModified: UpdateRenderTargets' PrepareImage drops the upload only when
         // IsFullClear agrees the clear covers the whole image, and uploads it otherwise.
+        if (depth_clear_relaxed) {
+            ++tc_depth_clear_skips;
+            tc_depth_clear_skip_bytes += new_image.guest_size_bytes;
+            if (SkipStaleUploads()) {
+                // UB-128: outside the clear's render area guest memory, not the GPU, holds this
+                // target's bytes, as the upload it replaces would have set: never marked stale.
+                new_image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::GuestBytes;
+            }
+        }
         runtime.TransitionImageLayout(new_image);
     } else if (copied_whole) {
         // What RefreshContents does, without the upload.
@@ -5674,6 +5718,36 @@ ImageId TextureCache<P>::JoinImages(const ImageInfo& info, GPUVAddr gpu_addr, DA
         }
         runtime.TransitionImageLayout(new_image);
     } else {
+        if (FritchiiDepthClear() && clearing_render_targets &&
+            new_image.guest_size_bytes >= 1_MiB && maxwell3d->regs.zeta_enable &&
+            maxwell3d->regs.zeta.Address() == gpu_addr) [[unlikely]] {
+            // EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR: why a cleared depth target was still uploaded.
+            static u32 depth_refusals_logged{};
+            if (depth_refusals_logged < 8) {
+                ++depth_refusals_logged;
+                const auto& regs = maxwell3d->regs;
+                const auto& surface = regs.clear_surface;
+                const auto& scissor = regs.scissor_test[0];
+                LOG_INFO(HW_GPU,
+                         "Depth clear: depth target format {} {}x{} levels {} layers {} samples "
+                         "{} at {:#x} uploaded: {} join copies, clear Z {} S {} layer {}, "
+                         "stencil mask {:#x}, scissor {} ({},{})-({},{}), rt0 {}x{} of {} "
+                         "targets, depth {}x{}, clear test passed {} (then a guard kept it)",
+                         static_cast<u32>(new_info.format), new_info.size.width,
+                         new_info.size.height, new_info.resources.levels,
+                         new_info.resources.layers, new_info.num_samples, gpu_addr,
+                         join_copies_to_do.size(), static_cast<u32>(surface.Z),
+                         static_cast<u32>(surface.S), static_cast<u32>(surface.layer),
+                         static_cast<u32>(regs.stencil_front_mask),
+                         static_cast<u32>(regs.clear_control.use_scissor),
+                         static_cast<u32>(scissor.min_x), static_cast<u32>(scissor.min_y),
+                         static_cast<u32>(scissor.max_x), static_cast<u32>(scissor.max_y),
+                         static_cast<u32>(regs.rt[0].width), static_cast<u32>(regs.rt[0].height),
+                         static_cast<u32>(regs.rt_control.count),
+                         static_cast<u32>(regs.zeta_size.width),
+                         static_cast<u32>(regs.zeta_size.height), overwritten_by_clear());
+            }
+        }
         // TODO: Only upload what we need
         RefreshContents(new_image, new_image_id);
     }
diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
index e6055b0..980da29 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache_base.h
@@ -199,6 +199,8 @@ class TextureCache : public VideoCommon::ChannelSetupCaches<TextureCacheChannelI
     u64 area_evicted_images{};  ///< This burst's totals (the done line)
     u64 area_evicted_bytes{};
     u64 area_dropped_images{};  ///< Of them, GPU-written images deleted without a copy
+    u64 tc_depth_clear_skips{};      ///< EDEN_UP_FRITCHII_DEPTH_CLEAR: join uploads left to the clear
+    u64 tc_depth_clear_skip_bytes{}; ///< Their guest sizes (last 600 frames)
     /// EDEN_NX2_CLEAN_BY_TIME: AreaEvict's window also ends no earlier than this (see AreaEvict)
     std::chrono::steady_clock::time_point area_evict_until_time{};
     u64 area_evict_min_until{}; ///< ...but not before this frame (very low frame rates)
